say which side of a sort holds the nil

-[NSMutableArray sortRange:options:usingComparator:] hands its permuted buffer to
replaceObjectsInRange, which raises "Cannot insert nil into array" if any entry is nil. The frames
then name only the sort, so an array that arrived holding a nil looks exactly like a sort that lost
an element, and the two want opposite work.

That cost a whole afternoon on Swift Publisher: Command Q raised here, the raise unwound out of
-[CCDocumentController applicationWillTerminate:], the run loop caught it, and the application
simply carried on without quitting. The answer, once measured, was nilsIn=1 with a valid
permutation: +[NSFontFamily allFontFamilyNames] had built the array around a font family that had
no name.

The scan is O(n) against a sort that is O(n log n), and it prints nothing unless something is wrong.

--- a/NSArray.m
+++ b/NSArray.m
@@ -662,9 +662,29 @@
         return (CFComparisonResult)comparator(objs[i1], objs[i2]);
     });
     assert(sizeof(id) == sizeof(CFIndex));
+    /*
+     * A NIL HERE RAISES INSIDE replaceObjectsInRange AND THE FRAMES NAME ONLY THE SORT, which is
+     * how -[NSFontFamily allFontFamilyNames] came to kill Command Q in Swift Publisher with
+     * "Cannot insert nil into array". Say which side holds it: the array we were handed, or the
+     * permutation this sort built.
+     */
+    NSUInteger nilsIn = 0, nilsOut = 0, badIndex = 0;
+    for (NSUInteger i = 0; i < count; i++) {
+        if (objs[i] == nil) nilsIn++;
+        if (indexes[i] < 0 || (NSUInteger)indexes[i] >= count) badIndex++;
+    }
     for (int i = 0; i < count; i++) {
         indexes[i] = (CFIndex)objs[indexes[i]]; // re-use indexes allocation
     }
+    for (NSUInteger i = 0; i < count; i++) {
+        if (((id *)indexes)[i] == nil) nilsOut++;
+    }
+    if (nilsIn != 0 || nilsOut != 0 || badIndex != 0) {
+        fprintf(stderr, "CIDER_SORT %s count=%lu nilsIn=%lu nilsOut=%lu badIndex=%lu\n",
+                object_getClassName(self), (unsigned long)count,
+                (unsigned long)nilsIn, (unsigned long)nilsOut, (unsigned long)badIndex);
+        fflush(stderr);
+    }
     [self replaceObjectsInRange:range withObjects:(id *)indexes count:count];
     free(indexes);
     free(objs);
